+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static HTML and browser modules; no build is required. Run `npm test` for the Node security tests.
+
+## Ordering integration
+
+`security.mjs` trusts exactly `https://orders.dailygrind.coffee` for ordering messages.
+Set `ORDERING_ORIGIN` to the deployed ordering service and `OWNED_SITE_DOMAIN` to a
+private registrable domain you control. Do not configure a public suffix or shared
+hosting suffix as the owned domain.
+
+The ordering window can send either of these payloads to the page's exact origin:
+
+```js
+{ type: 'order-status', message: 'Your coffee is ready.' }
+{ type: 'redirect', url: '/orders' }
+```
+
+Redirects must be HTTP(S), credential-free and schemefully same-site with the
+current page. Relative URLs resolve against the page URL. External HTTP(S) links
+receive `external noopener noreferrer`; unsafe link schemes are blocked on click.
+
+## Sandboxed widget
+
+The page loads `widget.html` with `sandbox="allow-scripts"`, without
+`allow-same-origin`. The first `init` message must come from that iframe's captured
+`contentWindow`. On browsers with the `Origin` API, the receiver pins its underlying
+opaque origin once; it rejects other frames and a new document origin even when
+the iframe's window identity remains the same. Accepted `status` messages contain
+a string `message`, rendered as text.
+
+Without `Origin`, the receiver pins the expected sender window on `init`, requires
+the serialized origin to be `"null"`, and rejects other windows. This fallback
+cannot detect navigation to a different opaque document within the same iframe;
+do not navigate or reuse the initialized iframe for untrusted content. Same-site
+URL checks use the explicitly owned domain; on other deployments the fallback
+conservatively permits only matching hosts and schemes rather than guessing public
+suffix boundaries.
+
+Tests cover URL parsing and fallback behavior directly. Native `Origin` contract
+tests use a test double because Node does not expose browser opaque-origin events;
+they do not claim browser compatibility verification.
